{"kind":"report","text":"Corrected-product advice: this exact successor is READY for the one final implementation artifact and formal exact-head review. Inspected exact commit dd38c8778e4152a666aafb6a424688c7de2a1d9e and the complete branch delta from 5d18fa8. go test ./..., go vet ./..., go test -race over the concurrent packages (engine, projection, inbox, query), and scripts/demo.sh all pass at that head.\n\nEvery item from report 7450a5f1 is verifiably addressed, each with a test:\n\nB1 resolved. transientProcessError classifies context cancellation/deadline and transient SQLite codes (BUSY, LOCKED, IOERR, FULL, and kin); Process records a gap only for deterministic failures, and Drain re-checks the frontier before detaching so a transient error leaves the obligation pending for retry. TestCancelledProcessingLeavesDeliveryPendingWithoutGap and TestCancelledDrainLeavesObligationPendingForRetry pin both layers.\n\nB2 resolved. Recovery is per-app: any failure to recover a projection marks it unavailable with a stable projection_unavailable refusal across query, schema, mounts, and activate (reset required), reported in status; the engine serves everyone else. TestUnavailableProjectionDoesNotPreventResidentRecovery covers it. Activation is now journaled two-phase: definition_activation_journal is written before any mutation, FinishActivation atomically flips the registry and clears the journal, and recoverActivations reconciles a crash window by inspecting the stable projection identity — finishing a completed switch or rolling files back and aborting. TestRecoveryFinishesResetJournalAfterFileSwitch proves restart chooses one complete identity-matching state.\n\nB3 resolved. Continue now takes the drained boundary and atomically clears gap state, resetting the frontier so a storage-compatible reactivation of a gapped tailapp explicitly skips the detached interval and rejoins future delivery. The extended gap test repairs the gapped app by continue, preserves its rows, and proves it resumes consuming.\n\nAll nine advisories landed: fixed candidate/previous paths with cleanup on failure, success, and recovery (the retired-database retention concern is gone — the previous file is removed after a finished activation); the resident worker drains in bounded 16-wave passes and re-signals, so status/query/shutdown reach the barrier under backlog; the query result carries the true inbox delivery head (clamped monotonic against the frontier); exports over application views are refused at compile time with a clear message; JSON-typed values always cross SQLite as JSON text, with a round-trip test; guard.jsonata now gates both consecutive-failure and no-progress counters on observed telemetry (separate action and progress fingerprints with progress_coverage), so gated harnesses cannot generate spurious loop findings; the expected-revision race test and the runtime-upgrade readiness test exist and pass.\n\nThe new deterministic query budget deserves one note for the record: it counts the pinned ncruces driver's fixed-cadence progress callbacks (every 1,000 VM instructions) through a budget context, which makes the ceiling deterministic only relative to that driver behavior — correctly documented in-code as part of the runtime profile, with the wall deadline retained as a secondary net. That is a sound v1 mechanism; revisit only if the driver pin changes.\n\nOne residual nit, not blocking: Continue resets interpreted_position to the activation boundary for every continuation, which is correct because activation drains under the engine lock, but the invariant (boundary equals the app's drained position) is implicit — worth one assertion or comment so a future scheduler change cannot silently skip records.\n\nProvenance is clean: the request cites the verbatim head, the head resolves, and the branch tip matches. Publish the final implementation artifact at dd38c8778e4152a666aafb6a424688c7de2a1d9e (or a trivial successor), and I am ready to file the formal exact-head review with an approved verdict barring surprises in the published artifact set."}